});
}

Choosing the Threshold
For any fixed threshold \tau, we label the predicted class by considering the following decision rule: 
\hat{y}_\tau(\bold{x})\coloneqq
\begin{cases}
{\color{red}\tt 1}&\text{ if } p({\tt 1}\mid\bold{x}) \geq \tau \\
{\color{green}\tt 0}&\text{ if } p({\tt 1}\mid\bold{x}) &lt; \tau
\end{cases}
 In most cases, the common choice for \tau is 0.5. However, different values of \tau can be when the default is not deemed ideal.
Change the default \tau below to see the changes inflicted on accuracy, precision, recall, etc.

